{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-connection-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-connection-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of categorical connections (up to gauge)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-connection-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-connection-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","connection","gauge"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalConnection.unique_up_to_gauge","text":"categorical-connection-unique.md","leanSource":"categorical-connection-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-connection-unique\"></a><p>Two <a href=\"#def:categorical-connection\" data-at=\"quantum-universes/qu-structures\">categorical connections</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_1, \\nabla_2</code> on the same QU differ by a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Ad}(A)</code>-valued <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>-form:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\nabla_2 - \\nabla_1 \\;\\in\\; \\Omega^1(A) \\otimes \\mathrm{Ad}(A).</code></pre>\n<p>This difference is a categorical gauge potential. The space of connections is an affine space over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^1(A) \\otimes \\mathrm{Ad}(A)</code>, making uniqueness hold up to gauge.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.6.4","page":"b/prop-categorical-connection-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":93,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":70},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalConne